# Story report

1. What the runs prove

Each claim below is checked over the flushed files; the verdict table (section 7) says whether it held.
An assertion checks one component's own numbers; an oracle check compares the proxy's numbers with an
independent record (the simulated clients, the fake Postgres or the load tool).

The report's structural checks:
- DuckDB: DuckDB is installed and is the pinned family 1.5.x (it reads the files)
- arguments: every argument is an existing directory
- runs: at least one run directory was found at or below every directory argument
- finished: every run directory has run.csv (the run finished)
- files: every run directory has metrics.csv and histograms.csv
- schema header: every file starts with the schema version 1 header
- schema guard: the complete runs pass test/analysis/guard.sql: schema version 1 in every row, no empty required field, one run.csv row and a distinct run id per directory, metric rows in every run, and every flush run.csv declares is in metrics.csv

Scenario e2e-queue-full:
- every metric its checks require is in the final flush of every run
- oracle completed.sql: e2e-queue-full: two components, one query: the proxy received exactly the requests the clients sent, and the requests it completed (relayed to their end marker) are the clients' successes plus the errors the database itself returned.
- assertion conservation.sql: e2e-queue-full: conservation per instance from the exported counters: received = accepted + rejected, accepted = completed + failed + shed, and queued and in flight are 0 in the final flush; something was received.
- assertion faults.sql: e2e-queue-full: more clients than connections plus queue: exactly the three over the bound were shed (53M01).
- assertion resets.sql: e2e-queue-full: resets completed + resets failed + connections closed at release + connections lent as is = leases ended = leases started; resets started = leases ended with a reset; nothing is resetting in the final flush.
- oracle rows.sql: e2e-queue-full: every proxy-made error a client saw is counted under its error-contract row, and every counted row for a request reached a client: shed = 53M01, unsupported-feature + unsupported-extended = 0A000, lost-after-read = 08006, lost-after-write = 08007.

2. How the data was collected

- Tiers: S (simulator: the real engine on the event loop with the fake Postgres and simulated clients), 2 runs, 4 flushes.
- Schema version: 1 (every file header and every row; any other version fails the report).
- Runs: 2 complete run directories of 3 found under 1 argument(s), 1 scenarios; 4 flushes in all, 2 to 2 per run; 1 to 1 instances per run.
- Rows: 2508 metric rows and 88 histogram bucket rows.
- Components in the final flushes: classifier, engine, fakepg, obs, sim, simnet, wire, workload.
- Source: each run directory holds the CSV flush of PLAN.md section 7.7 (metrics.csv, histograms.csv, run.csv;
  rows appended at every publish interval and once more at the end, run.csv written last). The files are read
  with DuckDB 1.5.x through test/analysis/views.sql; "final flush" is the last flush_seq of a run. A run's
  scenario is the scenario column of its run.csv.

3. Inputs

| scenario       | tier | runs | seeds | arms | flushes | instances |
|----------------|------|------|-------|------|---------|-----------|
| e2e-queue-full | S    | 2    | 1-2   | base | 4       | 1         |

Legend: one row per scenario (run.csv scenario), aggregated over its runs. tier: S simulator, R real, bench.
runs: complete run directories. seeds: lowest-highest seed. arms: the arms present. flushes: flushes written,
summed over the runs. instances: instances per run (the distinct values).

4. Coverage by scenario, statement class and outcome

4.1 Proxy requests by outcome (engine)

| scenario       | outcome   | total | runs   |
|----------------|-----------|-------|--------|
| e2e-queue-full | received  | 24    | 2 of 2 |
| e2e-queue-full | accepted  | 24    | 2 of 2 |
| e2e-queue-full | completed | 18    | 2 of 2 |
| e2e-queue-full | failed    | 0     | 0 of 2 |
| e2e-queue-full | shed      | 6     | 2 of 2 |
| e2e-queue-full | rejected  | 0     | 0 of 2 |

Legend: engine requests_<outcome> in the final flush, summed over the scenario's runs. received = accepted + rejected; accepted = completed + failed + shed. runs: runs where it is not 0, of the scenario's runs. Every outcome is shown.

4.2 Proxy-made replies by error-contract row (engine replies)

| scenario       | error-contract row | total | runs   |
|----------------|--------------------|-------|--------|
| e2e-queue-full | shed               | 6     | 2 of 2 |

Legend: engine replies by reason, the row of the error contract (docs/error-contract.md) the proxy answered with. Rows that are 0 in every run are left out.

4.3 Statements by class (classifier statements_by_class)

| scenario       | class       | total | runs   |
|----------------|-------------|-------|--------|
| e2e-queue-full | start-lease | 24    | 2 of 2 |

Legend: Query messages the classifier classified, by statement class (the outcome label). Classes that are 0 in every run are left out.

4.4 Statements refused by the reject list (classifier rejects)

(no rows: no run exports it)

Legend: Query messages refused by the reject list, by reason. Reasons that are 0 in every run are left out.

