4.6 Simulated clients: errors by SQLSTATE (workload errors_by_code)

| scenario       | SQLSTATE | total | runs   |
|----------------|----------|-------|--------|
| e2e-queue-full | 53M01    | 6     | 2 of 2 |

Legend: Error replies the simulated clients received, by SQLSTATE. Codes that are 0 in every run are left out.

4.7 Load tool: what was intended and what was sent (loadgen)

(no rows: no run exports it)

Legend: The load tool's own counters in the final flush. achieved on time = sent - late, to read against intended; a shortfall run is one with late + could_not_send > 0 (informative, not a check). queued and in_flight are gauges. Every value is shown.

4.8 Load tool: sent requests by final outcome (loadgen completed)

(no rows: no run exports it)

Legend: ok, db-error (the database answered with an error), refused (the proxy answered with an error), lost (no answer). Every outcome is shown.

4.9 Load tool: error replies by SQLSTATE class (loadgen errors_by_class)

(no rows: no run exports it)

Legend: Error replies by the two-character SQLSTATE class. Classes that are 0 in every run are left out.

5. Failed assertions, in full

- structure: finished
  claim: every run directory has run.csv (the run finished)
  1 items:
    e2e-queue-full/3/base: no run.csv (the run did not finish)

6. Oracle mismatches, in full

None.

